   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "as straw. Hence we must say that for want of fixity as",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "regards the smallness or largeness of the objects of desire",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "the position of the wealthy magnifies or lessens things ( i. e.",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "their value ).",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r3",
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "46. O king, if you wish to milk this cow-like earth, then",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "first nourish ( enrich ) the nation as they do the calf; when",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "the nation ( the people ) is being constantly enriched, the",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "earth, like the desire-granting creeper, yields a variety of",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "fruits.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r4",
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "47. Now truthful, now false; at one time harsh, at another",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "speaking sweetly; now cruel and merciful afterwards; now",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "parsimonious, but anon liberal; ever spending wealth and",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "ever gaining large sums of money—thus the policy of kings,",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "like a harlot, assumes a diversity of forms.",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 7,
     "text": "",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r5",
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "48. What is the use of those men becoming the king’s,",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "servants ( lit. resorting to the king ) who do not possess the",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "six qualities, viz. the power to command, fame, the protection",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "of Bràhmaṇas, charity, the enjoyment of pleasures and the",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "protection of friends.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r6",
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "49. Whatever amount of wealth, large or small, might",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "have been allotted to ( lit. written on the forehead of ) a man,",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "he certainly obtains even in the country called Maru; on the",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "mountain Meru he will not be able to get more. Have",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 7,
     "text": "patience then, and do not adopt a servile course of conduct",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 8,
     "text": "towards the wealthy for nothing. See that a jar draws ( lit.",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 9,
     "text": "",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 10,
     "text": "takes up ) the same quantity of water from a well as well as",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 11,
     "text": "from the sea.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r7",
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "50. Oh magnanimous cloud, who does not know that you",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "alone are the supporter of the Châtakas ? Why do you then",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "wait for our plaintive appeal ?",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r8",
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "51. Oh friend Châtaka, listen ( to me ) with an attentive",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
